Package: evaldrift
Type: Package
Title: Paraphrase-Drift Scoring for LLM Eval Sets
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("James", "Verlander", email = "scrapertweeter3@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Maintainer: James Verlander <scrapertweeter3@gmail.com>
Description: Paraphrase-heavy eval sets drift over time: answers get
    rewritten, questions get reworded, and nobody re-runs the comparison
    that justified keeping both versions. eval_drift() scores two texts
    with three plain similarity measures (word-shingle Jaccard,
    character-trigram Jaccard, normalized Levenshtein similarity) and one
    blended drift score. No model calls, no network access, pure base R.
    Companion to the eval-methodology writing on PastAGI
    <https://pastagi.com>.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
URL: https://pastagi.com
BugReports: https://github.com/scrapertweeter3-prog/evaldrift/issues
